WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.316
The second term at Redmond sped by as quickly as the first, and Anne enjoyed it thoroughly.

2
00:00:07.317 --> 00:00:11.668
She studied hard, for she wanted to win a scholarship in English.

3
00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:20.509
If she won it, the scholarship would pay for her tuition fees at Redmond College next year, and she would not have to use Marilla's savings.

4
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:28.052
Gilbert, too, was hoping to get a scholarship, but he still found plenty of time to drop in and visit Anne at her boardinghouse.

5
00:00:28.053 --> 00:00:34.501
He was Anne's escort to most college events, and Anne knew students gossiped about them being a "couple."

6
00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:39.803
The gossip made Anne furious, but she could not refuse Gilbert's company.

7
00:00:39.804 --> 00:00:46.497
He was her old friend, and she would feel bad declining his kind offers to accompany her to college events.

8
00:00:46.498 --> 00:00:50.145
Besides, he had stopped acting like a suitor toward her.

9
00:00:50.146 --> 00:00:55.550
Anne was very glad of that, though she did secretly wonder why he'd changed.

10
00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:59.693
Only one disagreeable incident spoiled that winter.

11
00:00:59.694 --> 00:01:06.143
One night Charlie Sloane asked Anne if she would promise "to become Mrs. Charlie Sloane some day."

12
00:01:06.144 --> 00:01:10.028
Of course, Anne knew that she could never marry Charlie.

13
00:01:10.029 --> 00:01:14.027
After all, he was not her romantic hero either!

14
00:01:14.028 --> 00:01:22.690
"Another unromantic proposal!" Anne sighed. " Where is my Prince

15
00:01:22.691 --> 00:01:26.942
Charming?" The next day Anne scurried into Priscilla's

16
00:01:26.943 --> 00:01:35.012
room. "Read that," she cried, tossing Priscilla a letter from Stella Maynard, who had been one of their friends at Queen's

17
00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:38.667
College. "Stella is coming to Redmond to study next

18
00:01:38.668 --> 00:01:44.852
year. Tell me what you think of her idea. I think it's wonderful, if it's

19
00:01:44.853 --> 00:01:48.748
possible." "Anne, I have a little plan," Stella had

20
00:01:48.749 --> 00:01:55.067
written. "You know how I hate boarding. I've boarded for four years and I'm so sick of

21
00:01:55.068 --> 00:01:59.096
it. I can imagine you are not a huge fan of boardinghouses

22
00:01:59.097 --> 00:02:04.821
either. Why don't you and Priscilla and I rent a little house somewhere in

23
00:02:04.822 --> 00:02:09.558
Halifax?" "I think it's a good idea," said Priscilla after she read the

24
00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:17.650
letter. "So do I," agreed Anne delightedly. "Let's go house-hunting at once, before exams

25
00:02:17.651 --> 00:02:22.739
start." "I'm afraid it will be hard to get a house that fits our budget," warned

26
00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.305
Priscilla. "We'll have to be happy with a shabby little

27
00:02:26.306 --> 00:02:35.099
place." Over the next few days, they saw many houses, but they were either too big, too small, too expensive, or too far from

28
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.361
Redmond. The house-hunting was not going

29
00:02:39.362 --> 00:02:48.303
well. A few weeks later, Anne and Priscilla were walking home the usual way, down Spofford Avenue, so that they could look at Patty's

30
00:02:48.304 --> 00:02:56.310
Place. As they stopped to admire the garden, Anne suddenly shouted, "Look, look! Am I seeing things,

31
00:02:56.311 --> 00:03:03.018
Priscilla? Look over there and tell me if it's true!" Priscilla looked where Anne was

32
00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:07.262
pointing. Over the arched gateway of Patty's Place dangled a little

33
00:03:07.263 --> 00:03:12.592
sign. It said "For Rent. Furnished. Inquire

34
00:03:12.593 --> 00:03:19.265
Within." "Priscilla," said Anne in a whisper, "is it possible we could rent Patty's

35
00:03:19.266 --> 00:03:29.309
Place?" "It's too good to be true, Anne. Fairy tales don't happen nowadays . . . But then again maybe they do," Priscilla replied excitedly.

36
00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:35.237
"Anyway, it's too late to knock on their door this evening. Let's come back tomorrow."

37
00:03:35.238 --> 00:03:39.238
Early the next evening, the girls went back to Patty's Place.

38
00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:44.289
They knocked on the door rather timidly, and then stepped into a large living room.

39
00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.251
Two old ladies sat by the fire.

40
00:03:47.252 --> 00:03:53.825
They were very similar, except that one looked about seventy years old and the other fifty.

41
00:03:53.826 --> 00:03:58.957
They were both knitting, and the older one invited Anne and Priscilla to take a seat.

42
00:03:58.958 --> 00:04:06.238
Behind each lady sat a large white china dog, with a green nose and ears and green spots all over.

43
00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:11.954
Anne liked the dogs straight away; they seemed to her like the guardians of Patty's Place.

44
00:04:11.955 --> 00:04:21.884
For a few minutes nobody spoke. The girls were too nervous, and the ladies were content to knit and wait for their guests to speak first.

45
00:04:21.885 --> 00:04:26.619
Anne glanced about the room. What a nice place it was!

46
00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:35.899
Finally she spoke. "We . . . we . . . saw your sign that this house is for rent," said Anne to the older lady.

47
00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:43.022
"Oh, yes," said Miss Patty. "I meant to take that sign down today."

48
00:04:43.023 --> 00:04:48.587
"Oh, are we too late?" asked Anne, barely hiding her disappointment.

49
00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:55.670
"No," Miss Patty said. "We have decided not to rent it after all."

50
00:04:55.671 --> 00:05:01.289
"What a shame!" exclaimed Anne. "I love this place so much.

51
00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:04.210
I really hoped we could have lived here."

52
00:05:04.211 --> 00:05:07.319
"You love it?" said Miss Patty.

53
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:15.627
"I really do love it," Anne said. "I've loved it ever since I first saw it last fall."

54
00:05:15.628 --> 00:05:19.117
"You're not just saying that you 'love it'?

55
00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:24.275
Young people 'love' everything these days," said Miss Patty.

56
00:05:24.276 --> 00:05:31.432
"No, I really adore this house. Priscilla and I walk by it often," Anne said.

57
00:05:31.433 --> 00:05:36.039
"If you love it, you can have it," said Miss Patty.

58
00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:43.551
"I decided today that I wouldn't rent it because we didn't like any of the people who asked to rent it.

59
00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:50.091
You are different. I believe you do love it and will take care of it."

60
00:05:50.092 --> 00:05:53.273
"If . . . if we can afford the rent.

61
00:05:53.274 --> 00:05:57.230
We have a limited budget," said Anne meekly.

62
00:05:57.231 --> 00:06:04.308
Miss Patty named the amount. Anne and Priscilla looked at each other, and Priscilla shook her head.

63
00:06:04.309 --> 00:06:13.409
"I'm afraid we can't afford it," said Anne, choking back her disappointment. "We're only students and we're poor."

64
00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:20.585
"What can you afford?" asked Miss Patty. Anne named her amount and Miss Patty nodded.

65
00:06:20.586 --> 00:06:23.654
"That will do. You can move in.

66
00:06:23.655 --> 00:06:27.786
We leave in two months, at the start of next term.

67
00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:32.876
You don't object, I hope, to this house being called Patty's Place?"

68
00:06:32.877 --> 00:06:37.995
"No, that's one of the nicest things about it," Anne said, smiling.

69
00:06:37.996 --> 00:06:48.519
Patty's Place was theirs. At least one small dream had come true!

